# Why an epidemic turns by itself
subtitle: "How an epidemic peaks and fades while the virus stays just as contagious: it burns through the very people it needs"

## Why an epidemic turns by itself
sources:
    - id: km1927
      title: A contribution to the mathematical theory of epidemics
      authors: Kermack WO, McKendrick AG
      year: 1927
      finding: 'The SIR model: an epidemic turns when the susceptible share falls below 1/R0, and ends before everyone is infected.'

